From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 05:23:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: look up a plain ARM64 process's assemblies as
 sysarm64_ on iOS

link_winsxs installs each Wine assembly for arm64 from the ARM64EC set,
which the ARM64EC ntdll takes for an arm64, amd64 or "*" request. The
aarch64 ntdll, which runs a plain ARM64 child (madeira-unix 0249), asks
for the same arm64_ assemblies: Wine's ARM64 notepad, whose manifest
names Common Controls 6, got the ARM64EC comctl32_v6.dll, which it cannot
load (c000007b from comdlg32's and notepad's imports), and exited with
c0000135.

The aarch64 ntdll now looks an arm64 assembly up as sysarm64_, which
link_winsxs installs from the aarch64 set with the manifest's
architecture still arm64, as 0056 takes such a process's system DLLs
from sysarm64. ARM64EC and i386 ntdll.dll are unchanged.

Linear: PLA-606
Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-30-native-arm64-child.md
Offered-upstream: no; the split ARM64EC and aarch64 sets are specific to the iOS port
---
 dlls/ntdll/actctx.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/actctx.c b/dlls/ntdll/actctx.c
index 03a4dfc..7cd2770 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/actctx.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/actctx.c
@@ -3198,6 +3198,25 @@ static WCHAR *lookup_manifest_file( HANDLE dir, struct assembly_identity *ai )
     char buffer[8192];
 
     if (!(lookup = build_manifest_filter( ai ))) return NULL;
+
+#if defined(__aarch64__) && !defined(__arm64ec__)
+    /* Playport: on iOS the arm64 assemblies are the session's ARM64EC set,
+     * which a plain ARM64 process cannot load; its aarch64 set is installed
+     * as sysarm64_ assemblies, as its system DLLs come from sysarm64. */
+    if (!wcsncmp( lookup, L"arm64_", 6 ))
+    {
+        WCHAR *native = RtlAllocateHeap( GetProcessHeap(), 0, (wcslen( lookup ) + 4) * sizeof(WCHAR) );
+        if (!native)
+        {
+            RtlFreeHeap( GetProcessHeap(), 0, lookup );
+            return NULL;
+        }
+        wcscpy( native, L"sysarm64_" );
+        wcscat( native, lookup + 6 );
+        RtlFreeHeap( GetProcessHeap(), 0, lookup );
+        lookup = native;
+    }
+#endif
     RtlInitUnicodeString( &lookup_us, lookup );
 
 #ifdef __arm64ec__
